    },
    "message": "Give event outcome texts one exit in Rust, compare them with the Python rules, and move the handlers' and information events' texts\n\ncore/errors.rs raises EventSuppressed and EventApplicationError with the rule's text and notes where\nit was made; benchmarks/rule_shadow/text_check.py runs the Python rule on the same input each time a\nkernel raises one, through a hook of kernel_first and the dispatch loop's direct calls. The kernels of\nhandlers.rs and information_events.rs now check in the Python rules' order and raise their texts\ninstead of refusing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K4QyYRukuCLBerKa4UYj4y",
